---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
<div class="ivf">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
<main>
<section class="hero"><div class="w hgrid">
  <div>
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href={T}>Fertility Treatment</a> / PGT Genetic Testing</nav>
    <p class="eye">Doctor-led · Evidence-based · Lahore</p>
    <h1>Preimplantation Genetic Testing (PGT) in Lahore</h1>
    <p class="sub">PGT checks a few cells from a Day 5 or Day 6 <a href={`${T}/ivf`}>IVF</a> blastocyst for chromosome errors (PGT-A), single-gene disorders (PGT-M) or structural rearrangements (PGT-SR) before the embryo is transferred. Combined with a single euploid <a href={`${T}/fet`}>frozen embryo transfer</a>, it helps you choose the embryo with the best chance of a healthy pregnancy. Dr. Kamran Saleem recommends it when your history supports it.</p>
    <p><a class="btn" href={wa}>Book a PGT consultation</a> <a class="btn ghost" href="#pgt-process">See the process</a></p>
    <p class="mini">Not sure PGT is right? Start with a <a href="/services/assessment">fertility assessment</a> or review your <a href="/services/assessment/hormonal-analysis">hormonal analysis</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hside">
    <ul class="facts">
      <li><b>60–65%</b> live birth per euploid transfer, under 35</li>
      <li><b>98–99%</b> NGS testing accuracy</li>
      <li><b>25+</b> years in reproductive health</li>
      <li><b>3</b> Lahore locations</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div></section>

<div class="w layout">
  <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page"><p>On this page</p>
    {toc.map(([id, l]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{l}</a>)}
    <a class="btn sm" href={wa}>Book now</a>
  </aside>
  <div class="content">
    <p class="review"><b>Medically reviewed:</b> Dr. Kamran Saleem (MBBS 1988; UK Diploma, University of Liverpool; PMDC registered) · Practice follows ASRM, ESHRE and WHO 6th Edition guidance · Last review November 2026 · <a href="/dr-kamran-saleem">About the doctor</a></p>

    <section id="what-is-pgt">
      <h2>What Is Preimplantation Genetic Testing?</h2>
      <p>PGT is a laboratory procedure performed on Day 5 or Day 6 blastocysts before transfer. A few cells are taken from the embryo's outer trophectoderm layer and screened for numerical chromosome errors (PGT-A), single-gene inherited disorders (PGT-M) or structural translocations (PGT-SR).</p>
      <p>In Pakistan, PGT with single euploid embryo transfer can raise live birth per transfer to about 60–65% and lower early pregnancy loss to under 8–10%. It is most useful for women over 35, couples with recurrent pregnancy loss and carriers of genetic conditions.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {typeCards.map(([h, p, i]) => <div class="card"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[i]} /></span><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p></div>)}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pgt-types">
      <h2>The 3 Types of PGT</h2>
      <p>Each test answers a different question, so the right one depends on your history.</p>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Full term</th><th>What it screens</th><th>Who it is for</th><th>Technology</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{types.map(r => <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td><td>{r[3]}</td><td>{r[4]}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p class="note">All three tests need an <a href={`${T}/ivf`}>IVF</a> cycle with <a href={`${T}/icsi`}>ICSI</a> and blastocyst culture.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="pgt-a-m-sr">
      <h2>PGT-A, PGT-M and PGT-SR Explained</h2>
      <h3>PGT-A: screening for chromosome errors</h3>
      <p>A human cell normally has 46 chromosomes (23 pairs). Errors during egg meiosis become more common with maternal age, and an embryo with extra or missing chromosomes often fails to implant or ends in early loss. PGT-A identifies euploid embryos for transfer.</p>
      <h3>PGT-M: preventing inherited single-gene disorders</h3>
      <p>If both parents carry the same autosomal recessive condition, each pregnancy has a 25% chance of an affected child. PGT-M builds a probe specific to your family so that only unaffected or carrier embryos are selected.</p>
      <h3>PGT-SR: managing balanced translocations</h3>
      <p>A parent with a balanced translocation is healthy, but their eggs or sperm often carry unbalanced material. PGT-SR distinguishes balanced from unbalanced embryos, which lowers miscarriage risk.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="indications">
      <h2>Who Should Consider PGT?</h2>
      <p>PGT is advised when your history suggests a higher chance of genetic or chromosomal problems.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {indications.map(([h, p, i]) => <div class="card"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[i]} /></span><h3>{h}</h3><p set:html={p} /></div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="callout"><b>Honest counseling.</b> PGT-A does not suit every patient. For younger women with many good embryos, the benefit is less certain, and Dr. Kamran will say so rather than add an unnecessary step.</div>
    </section>

    <section id="pgt-process">
      <h2>The PGT Pathway, Step by Step</h2>
      <p>A PGT cycle has six phases across the clinic and the laboratory. The biopsy and the transfer happen in separate steps, so your embryos stay frozen safely while results are processed.</p>
      <div class="ovwrap">
        <p class="ovtitle">PGT Process at a Glance</p>
        <div class="ovrow">
          {overview.map((o, i) => (
            <>
              <a class="ov" href={o.h}>
                <span class="ovl">{o.l}</span>
                <span class="disc"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" set:html={o.art} /></span>
                <span class="ovn">{i + 1}</span>
              </a>
              {i < overview.length - 1 ? <span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 36 22"><path d="M3 3l7 8-7 8M14 3l7 8-7 8M25 3l7 8-7 8" /></svg></span> : null}
            </>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="ovhint">Select a stage to jump to its full explanation below.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        {steps.map((s, i) => (
          <li class="step" id={`step-${i + 1}`}>
            <div class="media"><span class="ph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[s.icon]} /></span></div>
            <div class="body"><span class="num">Phase {i + 1} · {s.time}</span><h3>{s.t}</h3><p set:html={s.d} /></div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="biopsy-safety">
      <h2>Is Trophectoderm Biopsy Safe?</h2>
      <p>At Day 5/6 the embryo has over 100–150 cells, divided into the Inner Cell Mass (the baby) and the Trophectoderm (the placenta). The biopsy samples only trophectoderm cells.</p>
      <div class="cards">
        {safety.map(([h, p, i]) => <div class="card"><span class="ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" set:html={icons[i]} /></span><h3>{h}</h3><p>{p}</p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p class="note">Long-term follow-up studies have not shown an increase in developmental anomalies.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="success-rates">
      <h2>Euploidy Rates and Live Birth by Age</h2>
      <p>Older women produce fewer euploid embryos per cycle, but once a euploid embryo is transferred the outcome depends far less on age.</p>
      <div class="tw"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Age</th><th>Blastocyst euploidy rate</th><th>Live birth per euploid FET</th><th>Early loss risk (euploid)</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rates.map(r => <tr>{r.map(c => <td>{c}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody>
      </table></div>
      <div class="callout"><b>The "euploid equalizer."</b> After a euploid embryo is identified, live birth stays high, about 55–65% in the best age groups, because PGT-A bypasses the age-related drop in embryo chromosomes. The catch is that older patients may have fewer embryos to test, so more than one cycle can be needed.</div>
      <p class="note">Outcomes vary and no result is guaranteed. If transfer fails, see <a href={`${T}/fet`}>frozen embryo transfer</a> for next steps.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="mosaic">
      <h2>What If an Embryo Is Mosaic?</h2>
      <p>A mosaic embryo has a mixture of normal and abnormal cells. Modern NGS can estimate the proportion, for example low-level mosaic results below about 30–50%. Some low-level mosaic embryos have developed into healthy babies, but results are interpreted case by case.</p>
      <ul class="tick">
        <li>Euploid embryos are always transferred first</li>
        <li>Mosaic embryos are considered only after detailed genetic counseling</li>
        <li>Prenatal diagnostic testing is advised after any mosaic transfer</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="ethics">
      <h2>Islamic Compliance and Legal Framework in Pakistan</h2>
      <p>PGT follows Pakistani law and Federal Shariat Court rulings on assisted reproduction.</p>
      <ul class="tick">
        <li>Only the husband's sperm and wife's eggs are used within a valid marriage</li>
        <li>Donor gametes and surrogacy are not offered</li>
        <li>Screening to prevent severe inherited disease is widely supported by Islamic bioethics scholars</li>
        <li>Double-witness verification at every laboratory step</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="cost">
      <h2>PGT Cost in Lahore: Transparent Fees</h2>
      <p>A complete PGT cycle has four fee components, all explained before you begin. For the base cost see <a href="/resources/ivf-treatment-cost-in-pakistan">IVF treatment cost in Pakistan</a>.</p>
